>> title: Bánh Mì Không
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, vietnamese, rice flour, yeast, oven
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: banh mi khong, bánh mì không, Vietnamese baguette, banh mi roll, banh mi bread, Vietnamese bread roll, plain banh mi, empty banh mi, bread only, bánh mì thường
>> pairs-with: pork-liver-pate, do-chua
>> servings: 6
>> time: 4 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — a loaf proofed past forty-five minutes bakes into a soft roll, and the crust that makes it a bánh mì never comes
>> step.1: stir the sponge, ferment 2 hr
>> step.2: mix to a slack dough
>> step.3: knead 10 min, rise 1 hr
>> step.4: divide in six, shape, proof 45 min
>> step.5: slash, bake 475°F (245°C) 20 min with steam

Stir @bread flour{1%cup}(135 g), @cool water{2/3%cup}(160 g) and @instant yeast{1/8%tsp}(0.4 g) to a loose batter, then ~ferment{2%hr} until it domes and smells faintly sour.

Mix @&(~1)sponge{} with @bread flour{2%cup}(270 g), @rice flour{1/2%cup}(75 g), @warm water{3/4%cup}(180 g), @granulated sugar{2%tsp}(8 g), @fine sea salt{2%tsp}(10 g), @instant yeast{1%tsp}(3 g) and @ascorbic acid{1/8%tsp}(a crushed 500 mg vitamin C tablet).

Knead @&(~1)dough{} ~knead{10%min} until it is smooth but still slack and tacky, then ~rise{1%hr} until doubled.

Divide @&(~1)dough{} into six, roll each into an 8-inch torpedo tapered hard at both ends, and ~proof{45%min} seam down on a floured couche.

Slash @&(~1)rolls{} once down the length, slide onto a stone at 475°F (245°C) with a cup of water thrown in for steam, and ~bake{20%min} until the crust is pale gold.
